129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (Beta Thalassemia is an inherited blood disorder in which the body cannot make enough healthy haemoglobin, the protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen. As a result, children with severe forms of the disease develop anaemia and may require lifelong medical care. The disorder is caused by mutations in the HBB gene and is inherited in an autosomal recessive pattern, meaning a child must inherit one altered gene from each parent to develop the disease. Beta Thalassemia is one of the most common inherited disorders in Pakistan, affecting thousands of families nationwide.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
