177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (Cystic Fibrosis \(CF\) is an inherited disorder that causes the body to produce thick, sticky mucus. This mucus can block the lungs, digestive system, and other organs, leading to breathing difficulties, infections, and problems with growth. CF is caused by mutations in the CFTR gene and is inherited in an autosomal recessive pattern. A child must inherit one altered gene from each parent to develop the disease. Although Cystic Fibrosis is less common than Beta Thalassemia, it is believed to be underdiagnosed in Pakistan because many symptoms resemble common childhood illnesses.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
