231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (Lysosomal Storage Disorders \(LSDs\) are a group of rare inherited diseases in which the body cannot properly break down certain substances inside cells. Normally, tiny structures inside our cells called lysosomes act as recycling centres. They use special enzymes to break down fats, sugars, and other materials. In children with LSDs, one or more of these enzymes do not work properly. As a result, substances gradually build up inside cells and damage organs such as the brain, liver, heart, bones, muscles, and lungs. There are more than 50 different Lysosomal Storage Disorders, and symptoms vary depending on the specific condition. Although each disorder is individually rare, they are more common in populations where marriages between relatives are frequent because many are inherited in an autosomal recessive pattern.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
