286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Ehlers-Danlos Syndrome \(EDS\) is a group of inherited disorders that affect the body's connective tissues. Connective tissue acts like the body's support system. It gives strength and flexibility to the skin, joints, blood vessels, ligaments, and many internal organs. In people with EDS, changes in genes that help produce or organise collagen, the body's main structural protein, cause connective tissues to become weaker or more elastic than usual. As a result, individuals with EDS may experience unusually flexible joints, fragile skin, chronic pain, fatigue, and other symptoms that vary from person to person. There are several types of EDS, ranging from mild to severe. Some forms are inherited in an autosomal dominant pattern, while others are inherited recessively.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
